IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc6-builders`

-- ccc6-prohibition-orders.l4 -- s 161 (Order of prohibition: a person convicted of a sexual offence against a person under 18) and s 162.2 (Prohibition order: the Internet).
-- The court's duty to consider an order and its power to make one are two functions over the same gate. Both gates begin "When an offender is convicted ..." (a "when" gate):
-- a failed gate is JUST FALSE under ruling (b) of 2026-11-05, which counts "when" as "where" (fork F9: the power's other reading is NOTHING, the ruling of 2026-11-12, limit (3)).
-- The prohibitions of s 161(1) are in a list that has no "only": a prohibition outside it is NOTHING.

§ `s 161 Order of prohibition`

DECLARE `s 161(1.1) the offence charged` IS ONE OF
    `s 161(1.1)(a) an offence under this Act` HAS `the provision` IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `s 161(1.1)(b) an offence under the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read immediately before January 4, 1983` HAS `the section` IS A NUMBER, `the subsection` IS A STRING
    `s 161(1.1)(c) an offence under the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read immediately before January 1, 1988` HAS `the section` IS A NUMBER, `the subsection` IS A STRING
    `s 161(1.1)(d) an offence under subsection 212(1), (2), (2.1) or (4) of this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which paragraph (d) comes into force` HAS `the subsection` IS A STRING
    `s 161(1.1) any other offence`

-- (1.1) says "The offences for the purpose of subsection (1) are": read as closed, as the keel reads s 2.3(1) (fork F10): an offence none of (a) to (d) names is JUST FALSE.
-- src:3138 | Offences
-- src:3139 | (1.1) The offences for the purpose of subsection (1) are
-- src:3140 | (a) an offence under section 151, 152, 153 or 155, subsection 160(2) or (3), section 163.1, 170, 171, 171.1, 172.1 or 172.2, subsection 173(2), section 271, 272, 273 or 279.011, subsection 279.02(2) or 279.03(2), section 280 or 281 or subsection 286.1(2), 286.2(2) or 286.3(2);
-- src:3141 | (b) an offence under section 144 (rape), 145 (attempt to commit rape), 149 (indecent assault on female), 156 (indecent assault on male) or 245 (common assault) or subsection 246(1) (assault with intent) of the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read immediately before January 4, 1983;
-- src:3142 | (c) an offence under subsection 146(1) (sexual intercourse with a female under 14) or section 153 (sexual intercourse with step-daughter), 155 (buggery or bestiality), 157 (gross indecency), 166 (parent or guardian procuring defilement) or 167 (householder permitting defilement) of the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read immediately before January 1, 1988; or
-- src:3143 | (d) an offence under subsection 212(1) (procuring), 212(2) (living on the avails of prostitution of person under 18 years), 212(2.1) (aggravated offence in relation to living on the avails of prostitution of person under 18 years) or 212(4) (prostitution of person under 18 years) of this Act, as it read from time to time before the day on which this paragraph comes into force.
@ref Criminal Code s 161(1.1) (src:3138-3143)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 161(1.1) the offence charged`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 161(1.1) the offence is one referred to in subsection (1.1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN `s 161(1.1)(a) an offence under this Act` provision THEN
        IF    `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` provision 151
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` provision 152
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` provision 153
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` provision 155
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` provision 160 "(2)"
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` provision 160 "(3)"
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` provision 163.1
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` provision 170
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` provision 171
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` provision 171.1
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` provision 172.1
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` provision 172.2
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` provision 173 "(2)"
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` provision 271
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` provision 272
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` provision 273
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` provision 279.011
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` provision 279.02 "(2)"
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` provision 279.03 "(2)"
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` provision 280
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` provision 281
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` provision 286.1 "(2)"
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` provision 286.2 "(2)"
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` provision 286.3 "(2)"
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The offences for the purpose of subsection (1) are (a) an offence under section 151, 152, 153 or 155, subsection 160(2) or (3), section 163.1, 170, 171, 171.1, 172.1 or 172.2, subsection 173(2), section 271, 272, 273 or 279.011, subsection 279.02(2) or 279.03(2), section 280 or 281 or subsection 286.1(2), 286.2(2) or 286.3(2)"
    WHEN `s 161(1.1)(b) an offence under the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read immediately before January 4, 1983` section subsection THEN
        IF    section EQUALS 144 OR section EQUALS 145 OR section EQUALS 149 OR section EQUALS 156 OR section EQUALS 245
           OR (section EQUALS 246 AND subsection EQUALS "(1)")
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) an offence under section 144 (rape), 145 (attempt to commit rape), 149 (indecent assault on female), 156 (indecent assault on male) or 245 (common assault) or subsection 246(1) (assault with intent) of the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read immediately before January 4, 1983"
    WHEN `s 161(1.1)(c) an offence under the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read immediately before January 1, 1988` section subsection THEN
        IF    (section EQUALS 146 AND subsection EQUALS "(1)")
           OR section EQUALS 153 OR section EQUALS 155 OR section EQUALS 157 OR section EQUALS 166 OR section EQUALS 167
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) an offence under subsection 146(1) (sexual intercourse with a female under 14) or section 153 (sexual intercourse with step-daughter), 155 (buggery or bestiality), 157 (gross indecency), 166 (parent or guardian procuring defilement) or 167 (householder permitting defilement) of the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read immediately before January 1, 1988"
    WHEN `s 161(1.1)(d) an offence under subsection 212(1), (2), (2.1) or (4) of this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which paragraph (d) comes into force` subsection THEN
        IF subsection EQUALS "(1)" OR subsection EQUALS "(2)" OR subsection EQUALS "(2.1)" OR subsection EQUALS "(4)"
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) an offence under subsection 212(1) (procuring), 212(2) (living on the avails of prostitution of person under 18 years), 212(2.1) (aggravated offence in relation to living on the avails of prostitution of person under 18 years) or 212(4) (prostitution of person under 18 years) of this Act, as it read from time to time before the day on which this paragraph comes into force"
    WHEN `s 161(1.1) any other offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The offences for the purpose of subsection (1) are"

-- (1) the gate: "When an offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730, of an offence referred to in subsection (1.1) in respect of a person who is under the age of 18 years".
-- src:3131 | Order of prohibition
-- src:3132 | 161 (1) When an offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730, of an offence referred to in subsection (1.1) in respect of a person who is under the age of 18 years, the court that sentences the offender or directs that the accused be discharged, as the case may be, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed for that offence or any other condition prescribed in the order of discharge, shall consider making and may make, subject to the conditions or exemptions that the court directs, an order prohibiting the offender from
-- src:3133 | (a) attending a public park or public swimming area where persons under the age of 18 years are present or can reasonably be expected to be present, or a daycare centre, schoolground, playground or community centre;
-- src:3134 | (a.1) being within two kilometres, or any other distance specified in the order, of any dwelling-house where the victim identified in the order ordinarily resides or of any other place specified in the order;
-- src:3135 | (b) seeking, obtaining or continuing any employment, whether or not the employment is remunerated, or becoming or being a volunteer in a capacity, that involves being in a position of trust or authority towards persons under the age of 18 years;
-- src:3136 | (c) having any contact — including communicating by any means — with a person who is under the age of 18 years, unless the offender does so under the supervision of a person whom the court considers appropriate; or
-- src:3137 | (d) using the Internet or other digital network, unless the offender does so in accordance with conditions set by the court.
@ref Criminal Code s 161(1) (src:3131-3137)
GIVEN `the offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 161(1.1) the offence is one referred to in subsection (1.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the age in years of the person in respect of whom the offence was committed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 161(1) the court sentences or discharges the offender in the case the subsection describes` MEANS
        `the offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730`
    AND `s 161(1.1) the offence is one referred to in subsection (1.1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    AND `the age in years of the person in respect of whom the offence was committed` LESS THAN 18

@ref Criminal Code s 161(1) (src:3131-3137)
GIVEN `the offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 161(1.1) the offence is one referred to in subsection (1.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the age in years of the person in respect of whom the offence was committed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 161(1) the court shall consider making an order of prohibition` MEANS
    IF `s 161(1) the court sentences or discharges the offender in the case the subsection describes` `the offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730` `s 161(1.1) the offence is one referred to in subsection (1.1)` `the age in years of the person in respect of whom the offence was committed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When an offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730, of an offence referred to in subsection (1.1) in respect of a person who is under the age of 18 years, the court that sentences the offender or directs that the accused be discharged, as the case may be, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed for that offence or any other condition prescribed in the order of discharge, shall consider making"

@ref Criminal Code s 161(1) (src:3131-3137)
GIVEN `the offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 161(1.1) the offence is one referred to in subsection (1.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the age in years of the person in respect of whom the offence was committed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 161(1) the court may make an order of prohibition` MEANS
    IF `s 161(1) the court sentences or discharges the offender in the case the subsection describes` `the offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730` `s 161(1.1) the offence is one referred to in subsection (1.1)` `the age in years of the person in respect of whom the offence was committed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When an offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730, of an offence referred to in subsection (1.1) in respect of a person who is under the age of 18 years, the court ... may make"

DECLARE `s 161(1) what the order prohibits` IS ONE OF
    `s 161(1)(a) attending a public park or public swimming area where persons under the age of 18 years are present or can reasonably be expected to be present, or a daycare centre, schoolground, playground or community centre`
    `s 161(1)(a.1) being within two kilometres, or any other distance specified in the order, of any dwelling-house where the victim identified in the order ordinarily resides or of any other place specified in the order`
    `s 161(1)(b) seeking, obtaining or continuing any employment, whether or not the employment is remunerated, or becoming or being a volunteer in a capacity, that involves being in a position of trust or authority towards persons under the age of 18 years`
    `s 161(1)(c) having any contact, including communicating by any means, with a person who is under the age of 18 years, unless the offender does so under the supervision of a person whom the court considers appropriate`
    `s 161(1)(d) using the Internet or other digital network, unless the offender does so in accordance with conditions set by the court`
    `s 161(1) something else`

@ref Criminal Code s 161(1)(a) to (d) (src:3132-3137)
GIVEN `what the order prohibits` IS A `s 161(1) what the order prohibits`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 161(1)(a) to (d) the order may prohibit the offender from` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what the order prohibits`
    WHEN `s 161(1) something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an order prohibiting the offender from (a) attending a public park ... (d) using the Internet"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (a.1): "any dwelling-house where the victim identified in the order ordinarily resides": s 2 "dwelling-house" is a seam (an input of the answer of `s 2 dwelling-house`).
@ref Criminal Code s 161(1)(a.1) (src:3134)
GIVEN `s 2 dwelling-house: the place is a dwelling-house` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the victim identified in the order ordinarily resides there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is another place specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 161(1)(a.1) the order may prohibit the offender from being near the place` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the place is another place specified in the order` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 2 dwelling-house: the place is a dwelling-house` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the victim identified in the order ordinarily resides there` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of any dwelling-house where the victim identified in the order ordinarily resides or of any other place specified in the order"

-- "within two kilometres, or any other distance specified in the order".
@ref Criminal Code s 161(1)(a.1) (src:3134)
GIVEN `the distance in kilometres specified in the order, if it is not two kilometres` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 161(1)(a.1) the distance in kilometres` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the distance in kilometres specified in the order, if it is not two kilometres`
    WHEN JUST distance THEN distance
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 2

-- (2) "The prohibition may be for life or for any shorter duration that the court considers desirable and, in the case of a prohibition that is not for life, the prohibition begins on the later of (a) the date on which the order is made; and (b) where the offender is sentenced to a term of imprisonment, the date on which the offender is released ..."
-- src:3144 | Duration of prohibition
-- src:3145 | (2) The prohibition may be for life or for any shorter duration that the court considers desirable and, in the case of a prohibition that is not for life, the prohibition begins on the later of
-- src:3146 | (a) the date on which the order is made; and
-- src:3147 | (b) where the offender is sentenced to a term of imprisonment, the date on which the offender is released from imprisonment for the offence, including release on parole, mandatory supervision or statutory release.
@ref Criminal Code s 161(2) (src:3144-3147)
GIVEN `the prohibition is for life or for a shorter duration that the court considers desirable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 161(2) the prohibition may be for the duration` MEANS
    IF `the prohibition is for life or for a shorter duration that the court considers desirable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The prohibition may be for life or for any shorter duration that the court considers desirable"

@ref Criminal Code s 161(2) (src:3145-3147)
GIVEN `the prohibition is for life` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the offender is sentenced to a term of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the offender is released from imprisonment for the offence, including release on parole, mandatory supervision or statutory release` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 161(2) the date on which the prohibition begins` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the prohibition is for life` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says when a prohibition "that is not for life" begins and says nothing of one that is for life
        IF `the offender is sentenced to a term of imprisonment` AND `the date on which the offender is released from imprisonment for the offence, including release on parole, mandatory supervision or statutory release` AT LEAST `the date on which the order is made`
        THEN JUST (`the date on which the offender is released from imprisonment for the offence, including release on parole, mandatory supervision or statutory release`)
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the date on which the order is made`)

-- (3) "may, on application of the offender or the prosecutor, require the offender to appear before it at any time and ... may vary the conditions ... if, in the opinion of the court, the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances": a power of the court, with an "if" gate (11-12 limit (1)): NOTHING when it fails.
-- src:3148 | Court may vary order
-- src:3149 | (3) A court that makes an order of prohibition or, where the court is for any reason unable to act, another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province, may, on application of the offender or the prosecutor, require the offender to appear before it at any time and, after hearing the parties, that court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order if, in the opinion of the court, the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances after the conditions were prescribed.
@ref Criminal Code s 161(3) (src:3148-3149)
-- LIMB BY LIMB (sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F9): the application limb is a gate of the upon kind, so a failed application limb answers as the guide does (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05): JUST FALSE, listed in the fork register with the other reading (NOTHING). The other limbs are if-gates or scope limits and answer NOTHING (11-12 limit (1); ruling (c) of 2026-11-05).
GIVEN `the court is the court that made the order or, where that court is for any reason unable to act, another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the offender or the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the court the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances after the conditions were prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 161(3) the court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is made by the offender or the prosecutor`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the offender or the prosecutor"
        IF    `the court is the court that made the order or, where that court is for any reason unable to act, another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province`
          AND `in the opinion of the court the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances after the conditions were prescribed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, on application of the offender or the prosecutor, require the offender to appear before it at any time and, after hearing the parties, that court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order if, in the opinion of the court, the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances after the conditions were prescribed"

-- src:3150 | Offence
-- src:3151 | (4) Every person who is bound by an order of prohibition and who does not comply with the order is guilty of
-- src:3152 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than four years; or
-- src:3153 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 161(4) (src:3150-3153)
GIVEN `the person is bound by an order of prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does not comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 161(4) the conduct is the offence of not complying with an order of prohibition` MEANS
    IF `the person is bound by an order of prohibition` AND `the person does not comply with the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who is bound by an order of prohibition and who does not comply with the order is guilty of"

@ref Criminal Code s 161(4)(a) (src:3152)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 161(4)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 4, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 161(4)(b) (src:3153)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 161(4)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 161(4) (src:3150-3153)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 161(4) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- The prohibition of s 161(4) as a regulative rule: the person bound by the order (the offender) SHANT do what the order forbids. The text names the bearer, so SHANT is derived (ruling N2).
DECLARE `s 161(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 161(4) do a thing that the order of prohibition forbids`

@ref Criminal Code s 161(4) (src:3151)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 161(4) act`
`s 161(4) the offender SHANT do what the order of prohibition forbids` MEANS
    PARTY `the offender`
    SHANT `s 161(4) do a thing that the order of prohibition forbids`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the offender` BECAUSE "the offender did a thing that the order of prohibition under section 161 forbids"

§ `s 162.2 Prohibition order`

-- (1) "When an offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730, of an offence under subsection 160(3.1) or section 162.1, the court ... may make ... an order prohibiting the offender from using the Internet or other digital network".
-- src:3198 | Prohibition order
-- src:3199 | 162.2 (1) When an offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730, of an offence under subsection 160(3.1) or section 162.1, the court that sentences or discharges the offender, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed for that offence or any other condition prescribed in the order of discharge, may make, subject to the conditions or exemptions that the court directs, an order prohibiting the offender from using the Internet or other digital network, unless the offender does so in accordance with conditions set by the court.
@ref Criminal Code s 162.2(1) (src:3198-3199)
GIVEN `the offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162.2(1) the court may make an order prohibiting the offender from using the Internet or other digital network` MEANS
    IF    `the offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730`
      AND (   `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence` 160 "(3.1)"
           OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence` 162.1)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When an offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730, of an offence under subsection 160(3.1) or section 162.1, the court that sentences or discharges the offender, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed for that offence or any other condition prescribed in the order of discharge, may make"

-- src:3200 | Duration of prohibition
-- src:3201 | (2) The prohibition may be for any period that the court considers appropriate, including any period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment.
@ref Criminal Code s 162.2(2) (src:3200-3201)
GIVEN `the period is one that the court considers appropriate, including a period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162.2(2) the prohibition may be for the period` MEANS
    IF `the period is one that the court considers appropriate, including a period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The prohibition may be for any period that the court considers appropriate, including any period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment"

-- src:3202 | Court may vary order
-- src:3203 | (3) A court that makes an order of prohibition or, if the court is for any reason unable to act, another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province may, on application of the offender or the prosecutor, require the offender to appear before it at any time and, after hearing the parties, that court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order if, in the opinion of the court, the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances after the conditions were prescribed.
@ref Criminal Code s 162.2(3) (src:3202-3203)
-- LIMB BY LIMB (sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F9): the application limb is a gate of the upon kind, so a failed application limb answers as the guide does (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05): JUST FALSE, listed in the fork register with the other reading (NOTHING). The other limbs are if-gates or scope limits and answer NOTHING (11-12 limit (1); ruling (c) of 2026-11-05).
GIVEN `the court is the court that made the order or, if that court is for any reason unable to act, another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the offender or the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the court the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances after the conditions were prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162.2(3) the court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is made by the offender or the prosecutor`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the offender or the prosecutor"
        IF    `the court is the court that made the order or, if that court is for any reason unable to act, another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province`
          AND `in the opinion of the court the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances after the conditions were prescribed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, on application of the offender or the prosecutor, require the offender to appear before it at any time and, after hearing the parties, that court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order if, in the opinion of the court, the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances after the conditions were prescribed"

