-- src:3206 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than four years; or
-- src:3207 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 162.2(4) (src:3204-3207)
GIVEN `the person is bound by an order of prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does not comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162.2(4) the conduct is the offence of not complying with an order of prohibition` MEANS
    IF `the person is bound by an order of prohibition` AND `the person does not comply with the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who is bound by an order of prohibition and who does not comply with the order is guilty of"

@ref Criminal Code s 162.2(4)(a) (src:3206)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 162.2(4)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 4, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 162.2(4)(b) (src:3207)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 162.2(4)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 162.2(4) (src:3204-3207)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 162.2(4) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
